Aaargh!!!     I *LIKE* Omega VERY much, and I know that it's just a pre-
release...still.....

The game works well enough so that ones standards are heightened.
Take this for instance;  I'm walking merrily along a vast natural
cave the other day (just a couple of minutes ago actually) and
suddenly... out of the shadows a surprise attack!   No prob, I think,
just a Ninja or two..   Nosiree, 'twas a blasted Phantom!  He is
imprevious to all physical attacks (ok), and so I figured I'd give
him some righteous blast with my magic missile spell.  My mana was
high. No sweat.     Now, If I had actually seen the b....r verything
would've been fine. As it was the fouling fouler had *forced* me into
tactical combat mode  and was therefore NOWHERE TO BE SEEN.

How, I ask you, is a poor adventurer to know where to 'target' his spell
where no target is to be seen and at that had come 'from the shadows'
which could mean any direction at all.  As it was I only had time to
try three different directions before he 'sapped my very soul' out dry.

Don't misunderstand me now. Omega is the *absolutely* best game out I know
for any Unix system, closely followed only by Moria, even *with* it's
bu..err..features.   A small prayer for the creator only.. Make the
'combative' spells SELF-TARGETING in tac-mode.   Thank you.

Looking forward to next release,

